WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.875
Isn't my cat adorable?

2
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:17.375
She died recently. She lived for 12 years.

3
00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:25.166
I cried more for her
than when my husband died.

4
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.458
I felt heartless, like a terrible person.

5
00:00:30.958 --> 00:00:33.083
Which made the depression worse.

6
00:00:36.416 --> 00:00:39.708
I don't think tears are a measure of sadness.

7
00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:43.291
Perhaps it hurt you more
not a waste of a cat,

8
00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:47.375
but coming to terms with her husband's death.

9
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.166
You're right.

10
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.708
I still can't believe he's gone.

11
00:00:57.625 --> 00:01:00.291
I have the impression
that he wasn't back from work yet.

12
00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:03.625
I keep expecting
that he will come and say: "I am back."

13
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:10.375
I'm afraid that if I cry,
this will all become reality.

14
00:01:10.916 --> 00:01:13.375
Do you have another family?

15
00:01:14.041 --> 00:01:18.333
It helps in times like these
being around other people.

16
00:01:18.416 --> 00:01:22.375
Honestly, I have no contact with them.

17
00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:27.416
But recently my children
they visit me with their grandchildren,

18
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.041
thinking I'm lonely.

19
00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:31.583
And yet it's irritating...

20
00:01:31.666 --> 00:01:33.458
No, that's a bad word.

21
00:01:34.166 --> 00:01:36.583
I don't know how to behave around them.

22
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.750
Even in the family

23
00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:44.291
Building relationships takes practice.

24
00:01:47.041 --> 00:01:48.291
Exercise…

25
00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:54.583
Exercise…

26
00:02:02.791 --> 00:02:04.583
BOSS KENJI GAVE ME YOUR NUMBER.

27
00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:07.166
SORRY I'M LATE.
YOU FORGOT YOUR COAT.

28
00:02:10.125 --> 00:02:13.458
I'M SORRY I DIDN'T COME
AND I'M RESPONDING SO LATE.

29
00:02:16.416 --> 00:02:17.500
HIRO

30
00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:28.833
Yes?

31
00:02:29.833 --> 00:02:31.125
Hello?

32
00:02:31.208 --> 00:02:36.916
We were supposed to meet at Cielo on Valentine's Day.

33
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:37.833
Yes.

34
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:39.958
I know.

35
00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:42.666
Sorry for all these messages.

36
00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.333
I still have the coat you left behind.

37
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.833
If you don't mind,
I would like to come for him.

38
00:02:54.708 --> 00:02:57.958
Would you have time on Wednesday at noon?

39
00:02:59.666 --> 00:03:00.500
Yes.

40
00:03:01.083 --> 00:03:03.125
So let's meet on Wednesday at 12.

41
00:03:03.958 --> 00:03:05.208
In Cielo.

42
00:03:06.541 --> 00:03:07.375
All right.

43
00:03:18.791 --> 00:03:23.291
What am I thinking? I can't do it!

44
00:03:24.208 --> 00:03:27.125
What an idiot I am!

45
00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:30.958
PACAN

46
00:03:35.208 --> 00:03:36.166
Yes?

47
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.375
You immediately look grumpy.

48
00:03:39.875 --> 00:03:43.208
What is it about? I'm off today.

49
00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:45.208
Well…

50
00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:49.166
I was wondering
Would you like to exercise tomorrow?

51
00:03:50.541 --> 00:03:52.250
Exercise?

52
00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.708
Maybe we can go for lunch?

53
00:03:56.291 --> 00:03:57.333
What?

54
00:03:57.833 --> 00:04:00.333
We'd better eat separately.

55
00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:04.500
There is a restaurant
which I'm curious about.

56
00:04:04.583 --> 00:04:07.000
I finally managed to book a table.

57
00:04:08.125 --> 00:04:09.833
His name is Cielo.

58
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:11.416
Cielo?

59
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.666
- I'll hang up if you don't want to.
- NO!

60
00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.416
Sounds great.

61
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.000
Let there be Cielo!

62
00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:19.166
Yes, let's practice!

63
00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:42.833
ROMANTICS ANONYMOUS

64
00:04:42.916 --> 00:04:46.208
EPISODE 4
SWEET CHERRY BLOSSOM

65
00:04:46.833 --> 00:04:48.083
Good morning.

66
00:05:03.833 --> 00:05:05.416
Would you like to order?

67
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.666
I'd like an omakase tasting.

68
00:05:10.291 --> 00:05:11.583
Is it the same for you?

69
00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.125
- That's all.
- Of course.

70
00:05:15.208 --> 00:05:16.375
Thank you.

71
00:05:20.375 --> 00:05:21.208
True?

72
00:05:21.833 --> 00:05:24.000
What do you mean by that?

73
00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:27.375
Don't you feel comfortable around me?

74
00:05:28.291 --> 00:05:33.041
I am the only face in the world
that you can look at directly.

75
00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:36.791
Yes, that doesn't mean
that I want to look at her.

76
00:05:38.333 --> 00:05:44.416
So imagine a man
whom you like.

77
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.000
Sorry.

78
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.625
I need to use the toilet.

79
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:59.125
I don't even give a presentation.
Why am I sweating so much?

80
00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:15.666
Can I

81
00:07:16.916 --> 00:07:19.708
exercise again?

82
00:07:22.125 --> 00:07:22.958
Bright.

83
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.208
Go ahead.

84
00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:38.875
Sorry.

85
00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:42.666
What am I doing?

86
00:07:52.083 --> 00:07:53.666
Sorry about that.

87
00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.666
I thought you left.

88
00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.250
Of course not.

89
00:07:58.333 --> 00:08:00.291
You keep disappearing somewhere.

90
00:08:00.375 --> 00:08:03.750
Well... I have my reasons.

91
00:08:04.916 --> 00:08:05.875
Mr. Fujiwara.

92
00:08:06.833 --> 00:08:08.583
- Sorry.
- You'll forgive me.

93
00:08:08.666 --> 00:08:10.333
- Sorry.
- All right.

94
00:08:10.416 --> 00:08:12.750
- I met with your father.
- What?

95
00:08:14.791 --> 00:08:16.083
Good morning.

96
00:08:18.833 --> 00:08:22.083
This is Mr. Sasaki from Quick Mart Holdings.

97
00:08:22.166 --> 00:08:25.250
Nice to meet you. I'm Sosuke Fujiwara
from Futago Sweets.

98
00:08:25.333 --> 00:08:26.291
Sasaki.

99
00:08:27.208 --> 00:08:28.458
Nice to meet you.

100
00:08:35.708 --> 00:08:37.250
Nice to meet you.

101
00:08:37.333 --> 00:08:39.208
Mutually.

102
00:08:39.291 --> 00:08:42.500
Currently working
as my assistant in The Savior…

103
00:08:42.583 --> 00:08:43.416
Mr. Sasaki.

104
00:08:44.083 --> 00:08:46.500
- Thank you for meeting.
- Mutually.

105
00:08:49.666 --> 00:08:50.833
Sorry.

106
00:08:51.875 --> 00:08:53.208
Thank you very much.

107
00:08:57.791 --> 00:09:01.208
Sorry. Did I mess up?

108
00:09:01.291 --> 00:09:03.416
Whatever. I appreciate it.

109
00:09:14.083 --> 00:09:19.375
Who would have thought that a shared meal would be possible
will it be so difficult for us?

110
00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:21.041
I know.

111
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.291
Who would like to go on a date

112
00:09:25.708 --> 00:09:27.166
with someone like me?

113
00:09:30.291 --> 00:09:31.333
Well…

114
00:09:32.833 --> 00:09:36.333
If you like someone,
it wouldn't matter, right?

115
00:09:36.833 --> 00:09:40.041
Just so-so is enough
We'll sit quietly.

116
00:09:40.666 --> 00:09:42.125
Maybe, but…

117
00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.541
But it's too difficult.

118
00:09:48.291 --> 00:09:50.708
If, unlike you,

119
00:09:51.208 --> 00:09:56.583
he would be a nice handsome guy
with a pleasant scent,

120
00:09:57.208 --> 00:09:58.833
I would be very nervous.

121
00:10:00.791 --> 00:10:02.416
What?

122
00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:03.833
Wait a minute.

123
00:10:04.833 --> 00:10:08.875
So compared to a guy,
whom you like,

124
00:10:08.958 --> 00:10:11.750
I'm ugly

125
00:10:12.833 --> 00:10:13.916
unpleasant,

126
00:10:14.916 --> 00:10:16.291
and I stink?

127
00:10:16.375 --> 00:10:17.875
Of course.

128
00:10:18.375 --> 00:10:19.833
I don't stink at all!

129
00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:23.708
Maybe a little.

130
00:10:23.791 --> 00:10:24.666
What?

131
00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:28.000
I don't stink. Mercy.

132
00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.541
Maybe you too
doesn't know everything about this person.

133
00:10:32.041 --> 00:10:36.666
Observing it from a distance may vary
from meeting him in person.

134
00:10:39.166 --> 00:10:40.625
Is that what you think?

135
00:10:44.958 --> 00:10:45.791
Oh my?

136
00:10:46.458 --> 00:10:47.583
You've got something here.

137
00:10:51.375 --> 00:10:52.208
Here.

138
00:10:53.875 --> 00:10:54.791
Right here.

139
00:11:03.041 --> 00:11:03.875
Already.

140
00:11:12.208 --> 00:11:13.250
Yep, that's right.

141
00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:16.250
I'm sorry, are you okay?

142
00:11:17.375 --> 00:11:18.208
Absolutely…

143
00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:20.875
it's not okay.

144
00:11:28.958 --> 00:11:31.125
It's not easy at all.

145
00:11:46.458 --> 00:11:49.958
Doesn't this sound like a dating scene
from some romance?

146
00:11:50.625 --> 00:11:53.000
You leave behind an elegant restaurant

147
00:11:53.583 --> 00:11:56.333
and you eat burgers in the car.

148
00:11:56.416 --> 00:12:00.041
But for some reason
they taste even better.

149
00:12:00.625 --> 00:12:05.375
It seems like it's just you two
alone in the world.

150
00:12:05.458 --> 00:12:07.583
It's not like that. Don't stretch the truth.

151
00:12:07.666 --> 00:12:11.000
Before you knew it
you fell in love with her.

152
00:12:11.083 --> 00:12:11.916
What?

153
00:12:12.416 --> 00:12:15.041
She's already fallen in love with someone else.

154
00:12:15.125 --> 00:12:17.000
That's why we exercise.

155
00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.625
I really hope
that he will be with this person.

156
00:12:20.708 --> 00:12:23.250
So ro love triangle?

157
00:12:23.333 --> 00:12:24.333
Hey.

158
00:12:24.416 --> 00:12:28.500
This series is getting exciting!

159
00:12:32.125 --> 00:12:37.416
"If our liqueur is necessary,
I would like to meet the new president.

160
00:12:38.375 --> 00:12:40.958
It sounds polite, but it's actually a threat.

161
00:12:41.041 --> 00:12:42.375
What are we doing?

162
00:12:44.791 --> 00:12:46.250
Does it have to be me?

163
00:12:46.875 --> 00:12:48.041
Naoko Hosen.

164
00:12:48.791 --> 00:12:50.541
Proprietress.

165
00:12:55.791 --> 00:12:58.166
Oh boy.

166
00:13:03.291 --> 00:13:07.708
Sorry to disturb you.
I just got this letter.

167
00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:09.458
What is it about?

168
00:13:11.916 --> 00:13:15.750
What can you tell me?
about Gabriel Blossom?

169
00:13:16.666 --> 00:13:20.333
Apparently it's difficult to get along with their boss.

170
00:13:21.166 --> 00:13:23.500
She's raw and intimidating

171
00:13:23.583 --> 00:13:28.750
and choosing business partners,
he's mangling like he's at a job interview.

172
00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:33.458
I only heard about her from Kenji's boss.

173
00:13:33.541 --> 00:13:38.375
If her questions are not answered,
will not sign the contract.

174
00:13:38.458 --> 00:13:40.583
It's like a job interview.

175
00:13:40.666 --> 00:13:44.041
Asks about history, geography of the world,

176
00:13:44.125 --> 00:13:46.958
and even related matters
with environmental protection.

177
00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.083
Don't worry.

178
00:13:51.166 --> 00:13:54.416
Mr. Fujiwara graduated
prestigious university.

179
00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:03.208
Does it have to be Gabriel Blossom liqueur?

180
00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:05.208
Yes.

181
00:14:09.875 --> 00:14:12.291
I see. Thank you.

182
00:14:37.541 --> 00:14:39.791
CIELO At 12.00.

183
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.583
Boss Kenji,

184
00:14:47.666 --> 00:14:49.625
Wish me luck.

185
00:14:50.625 --> 00:14:52.833
I will try to be brave.

186
00:14:57.208 --> 00:14:59.625
TABLE MANNERS FOR ADULTS

187
00:15:21.333 --> 00:15:23.458
The only natural water liqueur in Tokyo,

188
00:15:23.541 --> 00:15:26.333
produced since 1965…

189
00:15:31.791 --> 00:15:34.875
YOU WILL GO WITH ME TOMORROW
TO GABRIEL BLOSSOM?

190
00:15:34.958 --> 00:15:36.416
YOU ARE SINGLE, RIGHT?

191
00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:39.875
NO. I ALREADY HAVE PLANS.

192
00:15:39.958 --> 00:15:41.958
IT WAS COLD.

193
00:15:57.375 --> 00:15:58.750
Nice color.

194
00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:00.708
So bright.

195
00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:05.291
I had a skirt around here somewhere.

196
00:16:06.541 --> 00:16:08.916
I wondered if I would ever wear it.

197
00:16:11.458 --> 00:16:12.416
This?

198
00:16:13.291 --> 00:16:14.250
Is this?

199
00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.083
This?

200
00:16:18.833 --> 00:16:21.500
- Welcome.
- Reservation in the name of Takada.

201
00:16:21.583 --> 00:16:23.750
We've been waiting for you. This way.

202
00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:50.875
What are you doing?

203
00:16:50.958 --> 00:16:52.250
Mr. Fujiwara?

204
00:16:52.333 --> 00:16:53.833
Please come with me.

205
00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:56.000
I'm listening?

206
00:16:56.541 --> 00:16:59.458
Let's go to Gabriel Blossom together.

207
00:17:00.708 --> 00:17:02.916
I said I wouldn't go.

208
00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.541
You're free, right?

209
00:17:04.625 --> 00:17:07.875
NO. I have plans.

210
00:17:11.041 --> 00:17:12.083
Please get in!

211
00:17:12.166 --> 00:17:13.125
What?

212
00:17:13.208 --> 00:17:15.041
You're stopping traffic.

213
00:17:17.708 --> 00:17:18.708
Faster!

214
00:17:20.916 --> 00:17:22.750
All right!

215
00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.958
You can't drag me along like this.

216
00:17:35.041 --> 00:17:38.833
Sorry. I couldn't go there alone.

217
00:17:38.916 --> 00:17:40.916
And I can't ask anyone else.

218
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:43.625
- What about Boss Motomi?
- It scares me.

219
00:17:43.708 --> 00:17:45.666
- And your secretary?
- At the headquarters.

220
00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.208
Why today?

221
00:17:48.291 --> 00:17:50.750
You don't want to help the Savior?

222
00:17:50.833 --> 00:17:53.166
I want to, but why today?

223
00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:57.416
Is it really more important
than the Rainbow Palette crisis?

224
00:17:58.708 --> 00:17:59.708
Ssagaji.

225
00:18:00.208 --> 00:18:02.125
- What?
- Please stop.

226
00:18:05.708 --> 00:18:07.625
Should I go?

227
00:18:08.125 --> 00:18:11.750
I could cancel a meeting over the phone,

228
00:18:12.666 --> 00:18:16.875
but I already posted it once,
so I feel terrible.

229
00:18:18.541 --> 00:18:21.250
I know I'm asking a lot...

230
00:18:22.958 --> 00:18:23.916
Well…

231
00:18:24.541 --> 00:18:27.958
I would step into your personal life,
so I can't.

232
00:18:28.041 --> 00:18:30.791
I can only ask you.

233
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:33.416
Please, doctor.

234
00:18:35.416 --> 00:18:39.125
I just have to say hello
and take him away, right?

235
00:18:41.583 --> 00:18:44.250
What is he like? How will I recognize him?

236
00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:46.208
No problem at all.

237
00:18:47.458 --> 00:18:49.000
He's handsome

238
00:18:49.666 --> 00:18:54.541
and it probably smells wonderful
even without a shower for several days.

239
00:18:55.041 --> 00:18:55.875
Yes.

240
00:18:55.958 --> 00:18:58.666
It's rare to find people like him,

241
00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:00.541
so you will recognize him immediately.

242
00:19:02.291 --> 00:19:06.375
Your heart seems to be beginning
open for me, Darth Vader.

243
00:19:06.458 --> 00:19:09.041
As a thank you for showing your face

244
00:19:09.125 --> 00:19:10.833
I'll go there instead of you.

245
00:19:10.916 --> 00:19:13.750
Really? Thank you very much!

246
00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.541
Ssagaji.

247
00:19:21.833 --> 00:19:22.708
Cheap.

248
00:19:23.208 --> 00:19:24.333
"Cheap"?

249
00:19:27.541 --> 00:19:28.916
Ssagajiro.

250
00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:31.375
Go shopping.

251
00:19:31.458 --> 00:19:32.458
I got scared.

252
00:19:35.416 --> 00:19:36.958
We can go.

253
00:19:37.041 --> 00:19:38.875
Everything's all right?

254
00:19:40.166 --> 00:19:41.000
One sec.

255
00:19:42.125 --> 00:19:44.166
Have you put on makeup?

256
00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.708
What if it's not okay?

257
00:19:46.791 --> 00:19:51.250
You were rushing me earlier,
because I was supposedly blocking traffic.

258
00:19:51.333 --> 00:19:53.333
Now you're pretending to be concerned.

259
00:19:59.916 --> 00:20:01.166
All right. Let's go.

260
00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:18.208
Welcome.

261
00:20:34.166 --> 00:20:35.458
Impossible.

262
00:20:36.833 --> 00:20:39.083
Can I help you?

263
00:20:39.166 --> 00:20:40.125
No, I…

264
00:20:50.583 --> 00:20:51.458
Okay.

265
00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.208
DR IRENE:
I'M SORRY. BUT I CAN'T DO IT.

266
00:21:19.708 --> 00:21:20.541
What happened?

267
00:21:20.625 --> 00:21:25.708
What should I do? This is the second time.

268
00:21:25.791 --> 00:21:28.250
He'll hate me.

269
00:21:28.333 --> 00:21:29.666
What happened?

270
00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:31.875
You didn't cancel the meeting?

271
00:21:32.541 --> 00:21:34.250
It's all your fault!

272
00:21:34.333 --> 00:21:37.833
What now? How will you fix it?

273
00:21:37.916 --> 00:21:39.791
Hey! Your phone is ringing.

274
00:21:39.875 --> 00:21:41.166
HIRO

275
00:21:44.541 --> 00:21:48.500
If he was that important to you,
you would call him.

276
00:21:53.791 --> 00:21:55.625
Please do it properly.

277
00:21:56.416 --> 00:22:00.208
If we lose this deal, I'll be furious.

278
00:22:00.291 --> 00:22:01.916
I'll be absolutely furious!

279
00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:05.083
Please look.

280
00:22:05.583 --> 00:22:06.666
It looks like snow.

281
00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:07.583
What?

282
00:22:10.958 --> 00:22:12.375
Gosh.

283
00:22:13.708 --> 00:22:14.958
How beautiful.

284
00:23:05.208 --> 00:23:06.416
Cedar ball!

285
00:23:10.833 --> 00:23:13.833
GABRIEL BLOSSOM

286
00:23:29.791 --> 00:23:31.500
Please wait here.

287
00:23:44.625 --> 00:23:46.541
Sorry to keep you waiting.

288
00:23:48.625 --> 00:23:53.125
Thank you very much,
that you came all the way here.

289
00:23:54.291 --> 00:23:55.958
Please sit down.

290
00:23:59.875 --> 00:24:01.250
I'm from Futago Sweets…

291
00:24:03.166 --> 00:24:06.791
I'm Sosuke Fujiwara from Savior.

292
00:24:06.875 --> 00:24:10.458
Nice to meet you. I'm Kiyomi Hosen.

293
00:24:14.416 --> 00:24:20.291
You were probably expecting my mother.

294
00:24:20.375 --> 00:24:22.208
I think so.

295
00:24:23.541 --> 00:24:24.750
Is he here?

296
00:24:26.958 --> 00:24:28.541
I'm so sorry.

297
00:24:30.208 --> 00:24:32.458
My mother, who founded this place,

298
00:24:34.125 --> 00:24:35.500
died.

299
00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:36.958
I'm listening?

300
00:24:37.708 --> 00:24:39.083
About two years ago.

301
00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:49.625
She left two orders in her will.

302
00:24:50.750 --> 00:24:51.958
First,

303
00:24:52.916 --> 00:24:58.041
when a business partner changes the president,
call him immediately.

304
00:24:59.583 --> 00:25:04.375
She had this extremely difficult test of hers.

305
00:25:04.875 --> 00:25:10.708
That's why I'm so brazen
we asked to come.

306
00:25:17.250 --> 00:25:19.125
Second command

307
00:25:20.166 --> 00:25:25.416
I was forbidden to talk about her death

308
00:25:25.500 --> 00:25:27.666
for at least three years.

309
00:25:28.416 --> 00:25:32.083
Otherwise the rumors would spread quickly,

310
00:25:32.166 --> 00:25:36.125
that the taste has changed or that the store has gone out of business,

311
00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:38.666
even if nothing has changed.

312
00:25:40.750 --> 00:25:42.875
We were told to wait three years

313
00:25:43.375 --> 00:25:47.916
before we announce that she died three years ago.

314
00:25:48.875 --> 00:25:51.250
If there was silence until then,

315
00:25:51.333 --> 00:25:53.000
it meant we won.

316
00:25:55.333 --> 00:25:56.500
Impressive.

317
00:25:58.750 --> 00:26:01.333
But I'm exhausted.

318
00:26:01.416 --> 00:26:06.125
I'm thinking about closing Gabriel Blossom.

319
00:26:08.250 --> 00:26:09.375
I'm listening?

320
00:26:09.458 --> 00:26:11.125
It's difficult, isn't it?

321
00:26:11.875 --> 00:26:14.291
Taking the place of the great founder.

322
00:26:15.791 --> 00:26:16.958
It seems…

323
00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:21.541
fighting a battle you can't win.

324
00:26:22.708 --> 00:26:24.250
A draw at best.

325
00:26:27.916 --> 00:26:29.458
Perhaps

326
00:26:30.250 --> 00:26:34.125
do you feel the same about the Savior now?

327
00:26:36.666 --> 00:26:37.791
That's true.

328
00:26:39.125 --> 00:26:39.958
But…

329
00:26:40.041 --> 00:26:43.291
I guess I'm tired of life

330
00:26:44.958 --> 00:26:47.208
dedicated to preserving tradition.

331
00:26:52.958 --> 00:26:53.791
Sorry.

332
00:26:56.583 --> 00:26:58.583
I believe the taste has changed recently

333
00:26:59.833 --> 00:27:01.625
is also perfect.

334
00:27:03.250 --> 00:27:04.083
I'm listening?

335
00:27:04.166 --> 00:27:08.208
It's different from your mother's recipe, isn't it?

336
00:27:09.291 --> 00:27:10.375
Most likely

337
00:27:11.958 --> 00:27:16.708
you changed the way of extracting the aroma.

338
00:27:20.083 --> 00:27:24.166
Did you notice this subtle difference?

339
00:27:25.958 --> 00:27:26.958
Yes.

340
00:27:27.041 --> 00:27:32.333
Compared to the original, I think
that new taste

341
00:27:32.958 --> 00:27:36.666
it is richer and better.

342
00:27:39.916 --> 00:27:43.250
Do you really think so?

343
00:27:44.083 --> 00:27:46.541
Yes. It is also more tart.

344
00:27:47.291 --> 00:27:49.333
If I had to describe it...

345
00:27:51.958 --> 00:27:54.458
It tastes like spring has come.

346
00:28:04.291 --> 00:28:06.125
I'm glad.

347
00:28:09.833 --> 00:28:11.750
This makes me so happy.

348
00:28:13.125 --> 00:28:15.875
Even though I knew it was the right move,

349
00:28:17.416 --> 00:28:23.083
changing my mother's recipe
it triggered me

350
00:28:24.458 --> 00:28:26.125
feeling of guilt.

351
00:28:28.666 --> 00:28:30.166
It was so painful.

352
00:28:33.666 --> 00:28:39.500
Maybe I'll stay a while longer
with your approach.

353
00:29:10.583 --> 00:29:12.291
You had a petal in your hair.

354
00:29:19.708 --> 00:29:22.666
What do you think this flower is?

355
00:29:24.541 --> 00:29:25.666
What?

356
00:29:27.166 --> 00:29:30.916
I tried to imitate
my mother's mischievous fun.

357
00:29:33.375 --> 00:29:37.750
Of course, these are not…
cherry blossoms, right?

358
00:29:38.250 --> 00:29:42.416
Most cherry blossoms have no fragrance,
so you can't get the flavor out of them.

359
00:29:42.500 --> 00:29:44.041
Right.

360
00:29:47.291 --> 00:29:48.916
So…

361
00:29:49.875 --> 00:29:51.916
The answer is…

362
00:29:52.916 --> 00:29:55.041
Apricot.

363
00:29:55.583 --> 00:29:57.541
- What?
-The answer is?

364
00:29:59.791 --> 00:30:01.083
Answer…

365
00:30:03.625 --> 00:30:05.458
my employee will give it.

366
00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:09.208
So what is it?

367
00:30:12.708 --> 00:30:14.416
Well…

368
00:30:14.500 --> 00:30:19.541
I guess you didn't order our liqueur,
without knowing the key ingredient?

369
00:30:20.375 --> 00:30:22.250
Well, no…

370
00:30:23.083 --> 00:30:24.125
I'll give you a hint.

371
00:30:24.625 --> 00:30:27.750
It's on the bottle of liqueur you're holding.

372
00:30:32.958 --> 00:30:35.708
Apricot.

373
00:30:37.500 --> 00:30:40.291
Apricot.

374
00:30:41.541 --> 00:30:44.375
Apricot?

375
00:30:45.416 --> 00:30:47.375
You passed.

376
00:30:49.541 --> 00:30:54.083
What's the name of the chocolate shop?
Which one are you opening?

377
00:30:55.208 --> 00:30:56.541
Savior.

378
00:31:00.041 --> 00:31:01.166
Come here.

379
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:09.958
To thank you for what you've done

380
00:31:10.500 --> 00:31:15.750
Would you like to be
our first customer?

381
00:31:27.791 --> 00:31:29.041
Gosh!

382
00:31:35.708 --> 00:31:37.916
So they weren't cherry blossoms.

383
00:31:38.875 --> 00:31:41.333
They were apricot flowers.

384
00:31:42.791 --> 00:31:45.833
the taste of chocolate,
that Kenji gave me as a child,

385
00:31:45.916 --> 00:31:50.041
he became for me
an unforgettable memory.

386
00:31:50.541 --> 00:31:56.375
A gift of chocolate for a child
it's the greatest pleasure.

387
00:31:58.375 --> 00:31:59.416
Well,

388
00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:04.958
if it's not Mr. Fujiwara,
and his employee was right...

389
00:32:10.250 --> 00:32:12.791
I've made my decision. You passed.

390
00:32:13.500 --> 00:32:15.291
We are truly grateful.

391
00:32:15.375 --> 00:32:17.291
Thank you very much!

392
00:32:17.791 --> 00:32:24.375
I will also support
new traditions of the Savior.

393
00:32:36.958 --> 00:32:37.958
Thank you.

394
00:32:38.541 --> 00:32:41.958
I knew it would be important to take a passionate person with me
it's a good decision.

395
00:32:44.250 --> 00:32:45.750
I'm glad it worked,

396
00:32:46.458 --> 00:32:51.458
but thanks to you
my love life is a complete mess.

397
00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:54.208
Really?

398
00:32:56.083 --> 00:32:58.000
If there's anything I can do...

399
00:32:58.083 --> 00:32:59.500
You can't.

400
00:33:08.166 --> 00:33:09.541
But before that

401
00:33:10.250 --> 00:33:11.916
I understood…

402
00:33:14.500 --> 00:33:17.125
that you have an amazing gift.

403
00:33:17.625 --> 00:33:21.916
You convey your true feelings.
Even though he can't look them in the eye.

404
00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:24.666
Even sitting next to me, I was moved.

405
00:33:26.875 --> 00:33:27.791
What?

406
00:33:29.458 --> 00:33:35.833
If you are confident,
your feelings will definitely reach him.

407
00:33:37.875 --> 00:33:40.875
Unless it's a ssagaji like me,

408
00:33:42.208 --> 00:33:43.208
only someone good.

409
00:33:50.083 --> 00:33:51.833
I wonder if I can do it.

410
00:33:53.708 --> 00:33:55.000
Gobaek.

411
00:34:02.125 --> 00:34:07.583
During the last session
we shared a sense of loss.

412
00:34:08.333 --> 00:34:14.250
This time I want you to share
positive feelings of love.

413
00:34:17.166 --> 00:34:18.708
Mr. Dear Tuna.

414
00:34:18.791 --> 00:34:21.541
If you've felt love lately,

415
00:34:21.625 --> 00:34:23.666
Would you like to tell us about it?

416
00:34:32.208 --> 00:34:34.958
Feelings of love…

417
00:34:47.458 --> 00:34:51.208
I've never felt anything like this.

418
00:34:51.291 --> 00:34:54.375
What? Impossible! Really?

419
00:34:54.458 --> 00:34:55.875
Poor thing.

420
00:34:56.375 --> 00:34:57.541
Are you okay?

421
00:34:59.416 --> 00:35:00.750
Thank you.

422
00:35:00.833 --> 00:35:03.791
Mr. Marumaru,
Will you be at the next session?

423
00:35:03.875 --> 00:35:05.083
Of course.

424
00:35:05.166 --> 00:35:06.083
Great. Me too.

425
00:35:06.166 --> 00:35:07.500
Mrs. Happy Cat.

426
00:35:08.750 --> 00:35:10.708
Please take this.

427
00:35:13.166 --> 00:35:16.916
Chocolates can help
in starting conversations with grandchildren.

428
00:35:17.958 --> 00:35:21.916
A gift of chocolate for a child
it's the greatest pleasure.

429
00:35:22.666 --> 00:35:25.666
Please offer them some
during your next visit.

430
00:35:26.208 --> 00:35:30.458
These are chocolates from the Savior,
in seven different flavors.

431
00:35:32.791 --> 00:35:34.125
From the Savior?

432
00:35:36.125 --> 00:35:38.416
Oh! If it's a problem...

433
00:35:38.500 --> 00:35:40.708
Whatever. I will accept them with joy.

434
00:35:42.250 --> 00:35:45.458
For the children and for me

435
00:35:46.041 --> 00:35:48.791
this will definitely be a great gift.

436
00:35:48.875 --> 00:35:52.000
Thank you. I appreciate it.

437
00:35:52.083 --> 00:35:53.166
I'm so happy.

438
00:36:09.375 --> 00:36:10.791
Gobaek.

439
00:36:13.750 --> 00:36:14.875
Confession.

440
00:37:12.458 --> 00:37:15.958
Sorry. Can I talk to you?

441
00:37:19.250 --> 00:37:22.083
Sorry I missed it
our meeting.

442
00:37:23.250 --> 00:37:26.625
I'm sorry I keep going
I'm leaving you to the wind.

443
00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:32.708
I want to tell you something.

444
00:37:35.250 --> 00:37:38.083
I…

445
00:37:47.833 --> 00:37:50.458
For a very long time…

446
00:37:53.250 --> 00:37:55.041
always…

447
00:37:56.208 --> 00:37:58.250
I always liked you!

448
00:37:58.333 --> 00:37:59.166
What?

449
00:38:46.708 --> 00:38:48.625
What should I do?

450
00:42:53.166 --> 00:42:56.000
Subtitles: Grzegorz Marczyk

